// Permit Read if an Alert with level exactly 3 happened within the
// last hour for the same principal. The predicate pins `level` to
// the integer literal `3` and omits `server` (which should be
// wildcarded). This exercises:
//   1. Integer-literal constant matching in the SQL WHERE clause.
//   2. Omission of the `server` field as a wildcard.
//
// trace_1: Three principals with different alert levels (1, 3, 5).
//          Only the principal who got level 3 has the Read permitted.
// trace_2: All alerts are non-3 (level 1, 5). No Read is permitted.
// trace_3: Alert fields in non-alphabetical order (server before
//          level). Verifies field-order independence for integer
//          literals.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Read",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Alert"::request{ input.level: 3, callerPrincipal: principal, callerResource: resource }
};
